{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Strong upward-trend underprediction: when the last 5–10 days show a persistent rise, add a positive level shift to the whole path (model is systematically too low by ~+2 to +12 EUR, with the gap widening with horizon).",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: apply an increasing uplift with forecast step (small at days 1–3, materially larger after ~day 7–10). The model’s slope is too flat versus realized outcomes.",
    "Lag in regime change: after a breakout to new highs, treat the model as ~1 week behind; pull forward the expected rise (front-load gains rather than spreading them evenly).",
    "Over-imposed mean reversion: if history is accelerating upward, reduce mean-reversion strength (do not fade back toward ~69–72); instead keep prices elevated and drifting higher.",
    "Post-spike behavior: the model anticipates dips/plateaus after local spikes that do not occur in outcomes; dampen any forecasted pullback unless history shows clear reversal signals (e.g., multiple down closes)."
  ]
}
